"45c_freecell.mst — FreeCell, the single-player card game, in the native Metal
 game pane (docs/gamepane_design.md). Launch it from the Demos menu, or a
 Workspace:

     FreeCell launch
     FreeCell launchDeal: 617     'the famously hard one'
     FreeCell launchDeal: 11982   'the one deal of the original 32000 nobody can win'

 DRAG a card (or a run of cards) with the left button and drop it where it
 goes; RIGHT-click a card to send it straight to a foundation if it will go;
 SPACE deals a new game; Escape quits.

 Why FreeCell rather than Klondike: every one of the 52 cards is face up from
 the first frame. There is no hidden information anywhere in the game, which
 makes it a far better demo — nothing is concealed, so nothing can be faked —
 and it makes the whole state assertable from a headless test.

 THE DEALS ARE THE REAL ONES, and this is checked rather than claimed.
 `dealNumber:` implements the Microsoft FreeCell shuffle to its published
 specification: the Microsoft C runtime's linear congruential generator,
 `state = (214013 * state + 2531011) mod 2^31` with the value taken as
 `state // 2^16` (so 0..32767); a deck ordered Ace of Clubs, Ace of Diamonds,
 Ace of Hearts, Ace of Spades, 2 of Clubs and so on, which is exactly
 `index = (rank - 1) * 4 + suit` for suits C, D, H, S; and the deal-as-you-go
 loop — pick the card at `random \\ remaining`, swap the LAST card into its
 place, deal the picked card — round-robin across the eight columns.

 Verified against the published reference deals for game 1 and game 617 (see
 `freecell_deals_match_the_published_reference_tables` in src/embed.rs): every
 card of both, in order, in the right column. So deal 617 here is deal 617
 anywhere, and the numbers people have traded for thirty years mean what they
 should.

 A note on reading those reference tables, because it cost a wrong conclusion
 once: they are printed as ROWS OF EIGHT in DEAL order, not as columns. Row
 one is the first card of each of the eight columns. Read down a printed row
 expecting a column and every deal looks subtly wrong.

 The one genuinely interesting rule is the supermove. FreeCell proper only
 ever moves ONE card; moving a run of n is shorthand for shuffling them
 through the free cells and empty columns, so it is legal only if
 (free + 1) * 2^empty >= n — and when the destination IS an empty column that
 column cannot also be used as scratch, hence 2^(empty-1). See
 `moveCapacityToEmpty:`.

 Drawing: the whole board is composed into one reused ByteArray of palette
 indices and blitted in a single command, recomposed only when something
 moves — which includes every frame of a drag, since the held cards follow
 the pointer. Ranks and suits are pixel art stamped into that same buffer
 rather than drawn with the pane's text overlay: the overlay is retained
 between frames, so redrawing 52 labels a frame would push thousands of
 commands a second down the VM->GUI channel (the mistake Minesweeper made
 once and this demo does not repeat).

 In a headless VM every game primitive silently fails, so loading this class
 outside the GUI is harmless — which is how its regression test drives it."
"I am FreeCell, played in the native game pane: 52 cards face up, four free
 cells, four foundations and eight columns. Launch me from the Demos menu, or
 a Workspace: FreeCell launch (or FreeCell launchDeal: 617 — my deal numbers are
 Microsoft's originals, checked card-for-card against the published reference
 tables, so they match everyone else's). Drag a card or a legal run with the
 left button; right-click a card
 to send it to a foundation; SPACE deals again; Escape quits. I move runs by
 the real rule — (free cells + 1) * 2^(empty columns) — and I send cards up
 automatically when it is safe to do so. Harmless to load in a headless VM."
Object subclass: FreeCell [
    | pane buf worldW worldH
      cols free found deal
      dragCards dragFrom dragIndex dragX dragY dragging
      moves won dirty rngState prevSpace prevRight |
    <classVars: Current>

    "── geometry ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     A card is 34x46 with a 38-pixel pitch, so eight of them span 300 of the
     320-pixel pane. FAN is the giveaway number: in a stacked column only the
     top FAN pixels of a covered card are ever visible, so the rank and the
     suit have to live inside that strip — everything else about the card
     face is decoration."
    FreeCell class >> cardW [ ^34 ]
    FreeCell class >> cardH [ ^46 ]
    FreeCell class >> pitch [ ^38 ]
    FreeCell class >> fan   [ ^14 ]
    FreeCell class >> originX [ ^10 ]
    FreeCell class >> topY   [ ^6 ]
    FreeCell class >> tableY [ ^62 ]

    "── palette ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"
    FreeCell class >> cTable  [ ^16 ]   "the baize"
    FreeCell class >> cFace   [ ^17 ]   "card face"
    FreeCell class >> cInk    [ ^18 ]   "black suits, card edge"
    FreeCell class >> cRed    [ ^19 ]   "red suits"
    FreeCell class >> cSlot   [ ^20 ]   "empty cell/foundation outline"
    FreeCell class >> cShade  [ ^21 ]   "card edge shadow"

    FreeCell class >> launch [
        "Deal a game from the wall clock — a different one every time."
        ^self launchDeal: (Time millisecondClockValue \\ 32000) + 1
    ]

    FreeCell class >> launchDeal: n [
        "Deal Microsoft FreeCell game number `n`. The same number always
         deals the same 52 cards, here and everywhere else."
        ^self new startDeal: n
    ]

    FreeCell class >> current [
        "The game most recently launched, so a Workspace can question it while
         it runs — `FreeCell current freeCellsUsed` — and so the regression
         test can read the board."
        ^Current
    ]

    startDeal: n [
        Current := self.
        pane := GamePane new.
        worldW := 320.
        worldH := 240.
        buf := ByteArray new: worldW * worldH.
        self buildPalette.
        self dealNumber: n.
        pane onStep: [ :frame | self stepWith: frame ]; run.
        ^self
    ]

    buildPalette [
        pane paletteAt: FreeCell cTable r: 0   g: 105 b: 60.
        pane paletteAt: FreeCell cFace  r: 250 g: 250 b: 245.
        pane paletteAt: FreeCell cInk   r: 20  g: 20  b: 25.
        pane paletteAt: FreeCell cRed   r: 200 g: 35  b: 40.
        pane paletteAt: FreeCell cSlot  r: 0   g: 80  b: 45.
        pane paletteAt: FreeCell cShade r: 0   g: 60  b: 35.
        ^self
    ]

    "── the deal ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    nextRandom [
        "Microsoft's LCG, exactly: state = (state * 214013 + 2531011) kept to
         31 bits, and the value is the TOP 15 bits of that. Getting either
         half wrong deals a plausible-looking game that matches nobody
         else's."
        rngState := ((rngState * 214013) + 2531011) \\ 2147483648.
        ^rngState // 65536
    ]

    dealNumber: n [
        "Deal game `n` and open it: the deal proper, then the opening
         auto-play (an ace at the foot of a column goes straight up — real
         FreeCell does this, and starting a game by clicking four aces is
         nobody's idea of play)."
        self dealRaw: n.
        self autoPlay.
        ^self
    ]

    dealRaw: n [
        "The deal exactly as the specification gives it, with nothing played:
         build the deck 0..51, then repeatedly pick the card at `random \\
         remaining`, swap the LAST remaining card into its place, and put the
         picked card onto the next column round-robin. This is the method the
         published reference tables are a statement about, which is why it is
         separate from the auto-play above.

         Card `c` is rank `c // 4 + 1` (1 = Ace) of suit `c \\ 4`, suits
         ordered C, D, H, S — i.e. the deck starts AC AD AH AS 2C …, as the
         spec requires."
        | deck j last |
        deal := n.
        rngState := n.
        cols := Array new: 8.
        1 to: 8 do: [ :i | cols at: i put: OrderedCollection new ].
        free := Array new: 4.
        found := Array new: 4.
        1 to: 4 do: [ :i | found at: i put: 0 ].
        deck := OrderedCollection new.
        0 to: 51 do: [ :c | deck add: c ].
        0 to: 51 do: [ :i |
            j := self nextRandom \\ (52 - i).
            last := deck at: 52 - i.
            (cols at: (i \\ 8) + 1) add: (deck at: j + 1).
            deck at: j + 1 put: last ].
        dragging := false.
        dragCards := OrderedCollection new.
        moves := 0.
        won := false.
        dirty := true.
        prevSpace := false.
        prevRight := false.
        ^self
    ]

    "── cards ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     A card is a plain SmallInteger 0..51 — no object, no allocation, and the
     rank and suit fall straight out of it."

    rankOf: c [ "1 = Ace … 13 = King." ^(c // 4) + 1 ]
    suitOf: c [ "0 clubs, 1 diamonds, 2 hearts, 3 spades." ^c \\ 4 ]
    isRed: c [ "Diamonds and hearts." | s | s := self suitOf: c. ^s = 1 or: [ s = 2 ] ]

    "── the rules ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    canStack: c on: onto [
        "Tableau build: one lower, and the opposite colour."
        ^((self rankOf: c) = ((self rankOf: onto) - 1))
            and: [ (self isRed: c) ~= (self isRed: onto) ]
    ]

    canFound: c [
        "A card goes up only onto its own suit's pile, and only next in
         sequence — an Ace onto an empty one."
        ^(found at: (self suitOf: c) + 1) = ((self rankOf: c) - 1)
    ]

    freeCellsUsed [ | n | n := 0. 1 to: 4 do: [ :i | (free at: i) isNil ifFalse: [ n := n + 1 ] ]. ^n ]
    freeCellsOpen [ ^4 - self freeCellsUsed ]

    emptyColumns [
        | n |
        n := 0.
        1 to: 8 do: [ :i | (cols at: i) isEmpty ifTrue: [ n := n + 1 ] ].
        ^n
    ]

    availableEmpties [
        "Empty columns usable as scratch. The column the run was LIFTED from
         does not count even when the lift emptied it: the cards are in the
         hand, not yet anywhere, and the rule is about the state the move
         starts from. Without this, taking a whole column and dropping it
         elsewhere would appear to gain a doubling it never had."
        | n |
        n := self emptyColumns.
        (dragging and: [ dragFrom = #column and: [ (cols at: dragIndex) isEmpty ] ])
            ifTrue: [ n := n - 1 ].
        ^n max: 0
    ]

    moveCapacityToEmpty: targetIsEmpty [
        "How many cards may travel as one run. FreeCell itself only ever
         moves a single card; a run of n is shorthand for parking n-1 of them
         in free cells and empty columns and putting them back, so the limit
         is (free + 1) * 2^empty. When the DESTINATION is an empty column
         that column cannot also be scratch, so it does not count itself."
        | empties cap |
        empties := self availableEmpties.
        targetIsEmpty ifTrue: [ empties := empties - 1 ].
        empties < 0 ifTrue: [ empties := 0 ].
        cap := self freeCellsOpen + 1.
        empties timesRepeat: [ cap := cap * 2 ].
        ^cap
    ]

    runLengthAt: colIndex from: idx [
        "How many cards from `idx` to the bottom of the column form a legal
         descending, alternating-colour run — 0 if they do not."
        | col n |
        col := cols at: colIndex.
        n := col size - idx + 1.
        idx to: col size - 1 do: [ :k |
            (self canStack: (col at: k + 1) on: (col at: k)) ifFalse: [ ^0 ] ].
        ^n
    ]

    "── moving ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    dropOnColumn: target [
        "Drop the held run onto tableau column `target`, if the rules and the
         capacity both allow it. Answers whether it moved."
        | col dest |
        col := cols at: target.
        dest := col isEmpty ifTrue: [ nil ] ifFalse: [ col last ].
        dest isNil
            ifFalse: [ (self canStack: (dragCards first) on: dest) ifFalse: [ ^false ] ].
        dragCards size > (self moveCapacityToEmpty: col isEmpty) ifTrue: [ ^false ].
        dragCards do: [ :c | col add: c ].
        ^true
    ]

    dropOnFree: target [
        "A free cell holds exactly one card, so only a single card may land."
        (free at: target) isNil ifFalse: [ ^false ].
        dragCards size = 1 ifFalse: [ ^false ].
        free at: target put: dragCards first.
        ^true
    ]

    dropOnFoundation: target [
        "One card, and it must be next in sequence for that pile's suit."
        | c |
        dragCards size = 1 ifFalse: [ ^false ].
        c := dragCards first.
        (self suitOf: c) + 1 = target ifFalse: [ ^false ].
        (self canFound: c) ifFalse: [ ^false ].
        found at: target put: (self rankOf: c).
        ^true
    ]

    sendToFoundation: c from: place index: idx [
        "The right-click convenience: put one card up if it will go, taking it
         from wherever it currently is. Answers whether it moved."
        (self canFound: c) ifFalse: [ ^false ].
        found at: (self suitOf: c) + 1 put: (self rankOf: c).
        place = #column ifTrue: [ (cols at: idx) removeLast ].
        place = #free ifTrue: [ free at: idx put: nil ].
        moves := moves + 1.
        Sound click play.
        self autoPlay.
        self checkWon.
        dirty := true.
        ^true
    ]

    autoPlay [
        "Send up everything that is unarguably safe, repeatedly. A card is
         safe when no lower card of the opposite colour could still need it —
         i.e. both opposite-colour foundations have already reached one below
         its rank. Aces and twos are always safe. This is the standard
         conservative rule: it never takes a card a later move might want."
        | moved |
        moved := true.
        [ moved ] whileTrue: [
            moved := false.
            1 to: 4 do: [ :i |
                | c |
                c := free at: i.
                (c isNil not and: [ (self canFound: c) and: [ self isSafe: c ] ]) ifTrue: [
                    found at: (self suitOf: c) + 1 put: (self rankOf: c).
                    free at: i put: nil.
                    moved := true ] ].
            1 to: 8 do: [ :i |
                | col c |
                col := cols at: i.
                col isEmpty ifFalse: [
                    c := col last.
                    ((self canFound: c) and: [ self isSafe: c ]) ifTrue: [
                        found at: (self suitOf: c) + 1 put: (self rankOf: c).
                        col removeLast.
                        moved := true ] ] ] ].
        ^self
    ]

    isSafe: c [
        "Safe to send up automatically: rank 2 or lower always, otherwise both
         opposite-colour piles must be at least one below this rank."
        | r a b |
        r := self rankOf: c.
        r <= 2 ifTrue: [ ^true ].
        (self isRed: c)
            ifTrue: [ a := found at: 1. b := found at: 4 ]      "clubs, spades"
            ifFalse: [ a := found at: 2. b := found at: 3 ].    "diamonds, hearts"
        ^a >= (r - 1) and: [ b >= (r - 1) ]
    ]

    checkWon [
        won := (found at: 1) = 13 and: [
            (found at: 2) = 13 and: [ (found at: 3) = 13 and: [ (found at: 4) = 13 ] ] ].
        won ifTrue: [ Sound powerup play ].
        ^self
    ]

    "── questions a Workspace (or a test) can ask ─────────────────────────"

    dealNumber [ ^deal ]
    moveCount [ ^moves ]
    hasWon [ ^won ]
    isDragging [ ^dragging ]
    columnSize: i [ ^(cols at: i) size ]
    cardAtColumn: i index: k [ ^(cols at: i) at: k ]
    foundationAt: i [ "Top rank on suit i's pile, 0 if empty." ^found at: i ]
    freeAt: i [ ^free at: i ]
    heldCount [ ^dragCards size ]

    nameOfCard: c [
        "A card in the notation everyone else prints — '7D', 'TC', 'AS'. Ranks
         are A23456789TJQK and suits CDHS, which is also the order the card
         index encodes, so this doubles as a statement of the encoding."
        ^(('A23456789TJQK' at: (self rankOf: c)) asString)
            , (('CDHS' at: (self suitOf: c) + 1) asString)
    ]

    columnString: i [
        "A whole column in reference notation, space-separated — what a test
         diffs against a published deal table."
        | s col |
        col := cols at: i.
        s := ''.
        1 to: col size do: [ :k |
            k > 1 ifTrue: [ s := s , ' ' ].
            s := s , (self nameOfCard: (col at: k)) ].
        ^s
    ]

    "Setting up a position — for a Workspace exploring an endgame, and for the
     regression tests. These bypass the rules on purpose: they place, they do
     not move."
    freeAt: i put: c [ free at: i put: c. dirty := true. ^self ]
    foundationAt: i put: r [ found at: i put: r. dirty := true. ^self ]
    clearColumn: i [ cols at: i put: OrderedCollection new. dirty := true. ^self ]
    clearFoundations [ 1 to: 4 do: [ :i | found at: i put: 0 ]. dirty := true. ^self ]

    "── input ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    stepWith: frame [
        "One frame. The board only recomposes when something moved — but a
         drag moves something every frame, so `dirty` is set while the pointer
         is down and holding cards."
        self readSpaceFrom: frame.
        self readMouseFrom: frame.
        dirty ifTrue: [ self paint. self drawHud. dirty := false ].
        pane present.
        ^self
    ]

    readSpaceFrom: frame [
        "SPACE deals the next game — on the EDGE, or holding it would reshuffle
         sixty times a second."
        | down |
        down := frame keyHeld: GamePane keyA.
        (down and: [ prevSpace not ]) ifTrue: [
            prevSpace := true.
            ^self dealNumber: (Time millisecondClockValue \\ 32000) + 1 ].
        prevSpace := down.
        ^self
    ]

    readMouseFrom: frame [
        "Left button: press picks up, holding drags, release drops. Right
         button: press sends the card under it to a foundation. Both are
         EDGE-triggered on the press — a held button must not pick up again
         every frame — while the DRAG itself reads the level, because
         following the pointer is exactly what a held button means."
        | left right wasRight |
        frame mouseInPane ifFalse: [ ^self ].
        left := frame mouseDown.
        right := frame mouseRightDown.
        wasRight := prevRight.
        prevRight := right.
        (left and: [ dragging not ]) ifTrue: [ ^self pickUpAt: frame mouseX y: frame mouseY ].
        (left and: [ dragging ]) ifTrue: [
            dragX := frame mouseX. dragY := frame mouseY. dirty := true. ^self ].
        (left not and: [ dragging ]) ifTrue: [ ^self dropAt: frame mouseX y: frame mouseY ].
        (right and: [ wasRight not ]) ifTrue: [ ^self rightClickAt: frame mouseX y: frame mouseY ].
        ^self
    ]

    pickUpAt: px y: py [
        "Take a card, or the legal run beneath it, off the board and into the
         hand. The cards leave their column now and go back on an illegal
         drop — which keeps drawing simple: what is in the hand is never also
         on the board."
        | where kind idx |
        won ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        where := self locationAt: px y: py.
        where isNil ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        kind := where at: 1. idx := where at: 2.
        kind = #free ifTrue: [
            (free at: idx) isNil ifTrue: [ ^self ].
            dragCards := OrderedCollection new.
            dragCards add: (free at: idx).
            free at: idx put: nil.
            dragFrom := #free. dragIndex := idx.
            ^self beginDragAt: px y: py ].
        kind = #column ifTrue: [
            | col k run |
            col := cols at: idx.
            col isEmpty ifTrue: [ ^self ].
            k := where at: 3.
            run := self runLengthAt: idx from: k.
            run = 0 ifTrue: [ Sound blip play. ^self ].
            dragCards := OrderedCollection new.
            k to: col size do: [ :m | dragCards add: (col at: m) ].
            run timesRepeat: [ col removeLast ].
            dragFrom := #column. dragIndex := idx.
            ^self beginDragAt: px y: py ].
        ^self
    ]

    beginDragAt: px y: py [
        dragging := true.
        dragX := px. dragY := py.
        dirty := true.
        Sound click play.
        ^self
    ]

    dropAt: px y: py [
        "Release. Try the slot under the pointer; if it refuses, the cards go
         back where they came from."
        | where ok |
        dragging := false.
        ok := false.
        where := self locationAt: px y: py.
        where isNil ifFalse: [
            | kind idx |
            kind := where at: 1. idx := where at: 2.
            kind = #column ifTrue: [ ok := self dropOnColumn: idx ].
            kind = #free ifTrue: [ ok := self dropOnFree: idx ].
            kind = #foundation ifTrue: [ ok := self dropOnFoundation: idx ] ].
        ok
            ifTrue: [
                moves := moves + 1.
                Sound click play.
                self autoPlay.
                self checkWon ]
            ifFalse: [ self returnHeld. Sound blip play ].
        dragCards := OrderedCollection new.
        dirty := true.
        ^self
    ]

    returnHeld [
        "Put the hand back exactly where it was picked up from."
        dragFrom = #free ifTrue: [ free at: dragIndex put: dragCards first. ^self ].
        dragCards do: [ :c | (cols at: dragIndex) add: c ].
        ^self
    ]

    rightClickAt: px y: py [
        "Send the card under the pointer up, if it will go."
        | where kind idx |
        (dragging or: [ won ]) ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        where := self locationAt: px y: py.
        where isNil ifTrue: [ ^self ].
        kind := where at: 1. idx := where at: 2.
        kind = #free ifTrue: [
            (free at: idx) isNil ifTrue: [ ^self ].
            ^self sendToFoundation: (free at: idx) from: #free index: idx ].
        kind = #column ifTrue: [
            | col |
            col := cols at: idx.
            col isEmpty ifTrue: [ ^self ].
            "Only the bottom card of a column can go up."
            (where at: 3) = col size ifFalse: [ ^self ].
            ^self sendToFoundation: col last from: #column index: idx ].
        ^self
    ]

    locationAt: px y: py [
        "What is under (px, py)? Answers #(kind index cardIndex) — kind is
         #free, #foundation or #column; cardIndex is which card down a column
         was hit, counting from 1. nil for the baize."
        | slot x |
        slot := (px - FreeCell originX) // FreeCell pitch.
        (slot < 0 or: [ slot > 7 ]) ifTrue: [ ^nil ].
        x := FreeCell originX + (slot * FreeCell pitch).
        (px - x) >= FreeCell cardW ifTrue: [ ^nil ].   "in the gutter between cards"
        py < FreeCell tableY ifTrue: [
            (py < FreeCell topY or: [ py >= (FreeCell topY + FreeCell cardH) ])
                ifTrue: [ ^nil ].
            ^slot < 4
                ifTrue: [ Array with: #free with: slot + 1 with: 0 ]
                ifFalse: [ Array with: #foundation with: slot - 3 with: 0 ] ].
        ^self columnHitAt: slot + 1 y: py
    ]

    columnHitAt: colIndex y: py [
        "Which card of a fanned column the pointer is on. Every card but the
         last shows only FAN pixels; the last shows its whole height."
        | col n top k |
        col := cols at: colIndex.
        n := col size.
        n = 0 ifTrue: [
            ^(py < (FreeCell tableY + FreeCell cardH))
                ifTrue: [ Array with: #column with: colIndex with: 1 ]
                ifFalse: [ nil ] ].
        top := FreeCell tableY.
        k := (py - top) // FreeCell fan + 1.
        k > n ifTrue: [ k := n ].
        k < 1 ifTrue: [ ^nil ].
        "Below the last card's full height is baize, not the column."
        py >= (top + ((n - 1) * FreeCell fan) + FreeCell cardH) ifTrue: [ ^nil ].
        ^Array with: #column with: colIndex with: k
    ]

    "── drawing ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    fill: px y: py width: w height: h color: c [
        "Fill a rectangle, clipped to the buffer — the dragged cards follow the
         pointer and can hang off any edge."
        | x0 y0 x1 y1 idx |
        x0 := px max: 0. y0 := py max: 0.
        x1 := (px + w) min: worldW. y1 := (py + h) min: worldH.
        y0 to: y1 - 1 do: [ :y |
            idx := (y * worldW) + x0 + 1.
            0 to: x1 - x0 - 1 do: [ :dx | buf at: idx + dx put: c ] ].
        ^self
    ]

    plot: px y: py color: c [
        (px >= 0 and: [ px < worldW and: [ py >= 0 and: [ py < worldH ] ] ])
            ifTrue: [ buf at: (py * worldW) + px + 1 put: c ].
        ^self
    ]

    paint [
        "Compose the whole board, then the hand on top of it, in one blit."
        self fill: 0 y: 0 width: worldW height: worldH color: FreeCell cTable.
        1 to: 4 do: [ :i |
            | x |
            x := FreeCell originX + ((i - 1) * FreeCell pitch).
            (free at: i) isNil
                ifTrue: [ self drawSlotAt: x y: FreeCell topY ]
                ifFalse: [ self drawCard: (free at: i) at: x y: FreeCell topY full: true ] ].
        1 to: 4 do: [ :i |
            | x r |
            x := FreeCell originX + ((i + 3) * FreeCell pitch).
            r := found at: i.
            r = 0
                ifTrue: [ self drawFoundationSlotAt: x y: FreeCell topY suit: i - 1 ]
                ifFalse: [ self drawCard: ((r - 1) * 4) + (i - 1) at: x y: FreeCell topY full: true ] ].
        1 to: 8 do: [ :i | self drawColumn: i ].
        dragging ifTrue: [ self drawHand ].
        pane blit: buf.
        ^self
    ]

    drawColumn: i [
        | col x y |
        col := cols at: i.
        x := FreeCell originX + ((i - 1) * FreeCell pitch).
        col isEmpty ifTrue: [ ^self drawSlotAt: x y: FreeCell tableY ].
        1 to: col size do: [ :k |
            y := FreeCell tableY + ((k - 1) * FreeCell fan).
            self drawCard: (col at: k) at: x y: y full: k = col size ].
        ^self
    ]

    drawHand [
        "The held cards, fanned under the pointer. Drawn last so they are over
         everything, and offset so the pointer sits near the card's top-left —
         where you grabbed it."
        | x y |
        x := dragX - 12.
        y := dragY - 8.
        1 to: dragCards size do: [ :k |
            self drawCard: (dragCards at: k)
                 at: x y: y + ((k - 1) * FreeCell fan)
                 full: k = dragCards size ].
        ^self
    ]

    drawSlotAt: x y: y [
        "An empty cell or column: a darker rectangle with a light outline."
        self fill: x y: y width: FreeCell cardW height: FreeCell cardH color: FreeCell cShade.
        self fill: x y: y width: FreeCell cardW height: 1 color: FreeCell cSlot.
        self fill: x y: y + FreeCell cardH - 1 width: FreeCell cardW height: 1 color: FreeCell cSlot.
        self fill: x y: y width: 1 height: FreeCell cardH color: FreeCell cSlot.
        self fill: x + FreeCell cardW - 1 y: y width: 1 height: FreeCell cardH color: FreeCell cSlot.
        ^self
    ]

    drawFoundationSlotAt: x y: y suit: s [
        "An empty foundation shows its suit, faintly, so you know where each
         one goes before anything is on it."
        self drawSlotAt: x y: y.
        self stamp: (self suitArt: s) at: x + 13 y: y + 18 color: FreeCell cSlot.
        ^self
    ]

    drawCard: c at: x y: y full: isFull [
        "A card. `isFull` draws the whole face; otherwise only the top FAN
         pixels will ever be seen, but the face is drawn anyway — the card
         below overwrites the rest, and one code path is worth more than the
         handful of stores it costs.

         The rank and the suit go in the top-left, INSIDE the fan strip: in a
         stacked column that strip is the only part of a covered card you can
         see, so anything drawn lower is decoration for the bottom card
         alone."
        | h ink |
        h := isFull ifTrue: [ FreeCell cardH ] ifFalse: [ FreeCell fan + 2 ].
        self fill: x y: y width: FreeCell cardW height: h color: FreeCell cFace.
        "A one-pixel edge, and the corners knocked off so it reads as a card."
        self fill: x y: y width: FreeCell cardW height: 1 color: FreeCell cInk.
        self fill: x y: y width: 1 height: h color: FreeCell cInk.
        self fill: x + FreeCell cardW - 1 y: y width: 1 height: h color: FreeCell cInk.
        isFull ifTrue: [
            self fill: x y: y + h - 1 width: FreeCell cardW height: 1 color: FreeCell cInk ].
        self plot: x y: y color: FreeCell cTable.
        self plot: x + FreeCell cardW - 1 y: y color: FreeCell cTable.
        ink := (self isRed: c) ifTrue: [ FreeCell cRed ] ifFalse: [ FreeCell cInk ].
        self drawRank: (self rankOf: c) at: x + 3 y: y + 4 color: ink.
        self stamp: (self suitArt: (self suitOf: c)) at: x + 22 y: y + 4 color: ink.
        ^self
    ]

    drawRank: r at: x y: y color: ink [
        "A for ace, J/Q/K for the court cards, 10 as two glyphs, the rest as
         one digit."
        r = 10
            ifTrue: [
                self stamp: (self glyph: 1) at: x y: y color: ink.
                self stamp: (self glyph: 0) at: x + 6 y: y color: ink ]
            ifFalse: [ self stamp: (self glyphForRank: r) at: x y: y color: ink ].
        ^self
    ]

    glyphForRank: r [
        r = 1 ifTrue: [ ^self glyphA ].
        r = 11 ifTrue: [ ^self glyphJ ].
        r = 12 ifTrue: [ ^self glyphQ ].
        r = 13 ifTrue: [ ^self glyphK ].
        ^self glyph: r
    ]

    stamp: rows at: px y: py color: c [
        "Draw pixel art — an Array of equal-length row Strings, `#` set and
         `.` transparent — into the frame buffer. `=` not `==`: String>>at:
         answers a fresh Character, not the canonical one, so identity is
         false even for the same character (the bug that made every piece of
         Minesweeper's art silently invisible)."
        | row |
        1 to: rows size do: [ :r |
            row := rows at: r.
            1 to: row size do: [ :k |
                (row at: k) = $# ifTrue: [
                    self plot: px + k - 1 y: py + r - 1 color: c ] ] ].
        ^self
    ]

    "── the pixel art ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    suitArt: s [
        "Clubs, diamonds, hearts, spades — 7x7, in that order (the order the
         card index encodes)."
        | a |
        a := OrderedCollection new.
        s = 1 ifTrue: [
            a add: '...#...'. a add: '..###..'. a add: '.#####.'. a add: '#######'.
            a add: '.#####.'. a add: '..###..'. a add: '...#...'. ^a asArray ].
        s = 2 ifTrue: [
            a add: '.##.##.'. a add: '#######'. a add: '#######'. a add: '#######'.
            a add: '.#####.'. a add: '..###..'. a add: '...#...'. ^a asArray ].
        s = 3 ifTrue: [
            a add: '...#...'. a add: '..###..'. a add: '.#####.'. a add: '#######'.
            a add: '#######'. a add: '.#.#.#.'. a add: '..###..'. ^a asArray ].
        a add: '..###..'. a add: '..###..'. a add: '#######'. a add: '#######'.
        a add: '#.###.#'. a add: '...#...'. a add: '..###..'. ^a asArray
    ]

    glyph: n [
        "Digits 0..9 as 5x7."
        | a |
        a := OrderedCollection new.
        n = 0 ifTrue: [
            a add: '.###.'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '#..##'. a add: '#.#.#'.
            a add: '##..#'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '.###.'. ^a asArray ].
        n = 1 ifTrue: [
            a add: '..#..'. a add: '.##..'. a add: '..#..'. a add: '..#..'.
            a add: '..#..'. a add: '..#..'. a add: '.###.'. ^a asArray ].
        n = 2 ifTrue: [
            a add: '.###.'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '....#'. a add: '...#.'.
            a add: '..#..'. a add: '.#...'. a add: '#####'. ^a asArray ].
        n = 3 ifTrue: [
            a add: '.###.'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '....#'. a add: '..##.'.
            a add: '....#'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '.###.'. ^a asArray ].
        n = 4 ifTrue: [
            a add: '...#.'. a add: '..##.'. a add: '.#.#.'. a add: '#..#.'.
            a add: '#####'. a add: '...#.'. a add: '...#.'. ^a asArray ].
        n = 5 ifTrue: [
            a add: '#####'. a add: '#....'. a add: '####.'. a add: '....#'.
            a add: '....#'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '.###.'. ^a asArray ].
        n = 6 ifTrue: [
            a add: '..##.'. a add: '.#...'. a add: '#....'. a add: '####.'.
            a add: '#...#'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '.###.'. ^a asArray ].
        n = 7 ifTrue: [
            a add: '#####'. a add: '....#'. a add: '...#.'. a add: '..#..'.
            a add: '.#...'. a add: '.#...'. a add: '.#...'. ^a asArray ].
        n = 8 ifTrue: [
            a add: '.###.'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '.###.'.
            a add: '#...#'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '.###.'. ^a asArray ].
        a add: '.###.'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '.####'.
        a add: '....#'. a add: '...#.'. a add: '.##..'. ^a asArray
    ]

    glyphA [
        | a |
        a := OrderedCollection new.
        a add: '..#..'. a add: '.#.#.'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '#...#'.
        a add: '#####'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '#...#'. ^a asArray
    ]

    glyphJ [
        | a |
        a := OrderedCollection new.
        a add: '....#'. a add: '....#'. a add: '....#'. a add: '....#'.
        a add: '#...#'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '.###.'. ^a asArray
    ]

    glyphQ [
        | a |
        a := OrderedCollection new.
        a add: '.###.'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '#...#'. a add: '#...#'.
        a add: '#.#.#'. a add: '#..#.'. a add: '.##.#'. ^a asArray
    ]

    glyphK [
        | a |
        a := OrderedCollection new.
        a add: '#...#'. a add: '#..#.'. a add: '#.#..'. a add: '##...'.
        a add: '#.#..'. a add: '#..#.'. a add: '#...#'. ^a asArray
    ]

    "── the HUD ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────"

    drawHud [
        "The text overlay, in viewport coordinates and retained between
         frames, so it is cleared and redrawn whole — and only when the board
         is redrawn."
        pane textClear.
        won
            ifTrue: [ pane text: 'YOU WIN' x: 128 y: 112 r: 255 g: 240 b: 120 scale: 2 ]
            ifFalse: [ ].
        "Both lines have to fit 320 pixels: the 5x7 font steps 6 pixels a
         character, so 53 characters is the whole width and the pane clips
         what runs past it without a word of complaint."
        pane text: 'DEAL ', deal printString, '  MOVES ', moves printString
             x: 4 y: 232 r: 200 g: 230 b: 210 scale: 1.
        pane text: 'DRAG   RIGHT UP   ESC QUIT'
             x: 158 y: 232 r: 140 g: 180 b: 160 scale: 1.
        ^self
    ]
]
